<title>USA: Group holds 9.1 pct Consolidated Cigar stake.</title>
<headline>Group holds 9.1 pct Consolidated Cigar stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Zweig-DiMenna Special Opportunties L.P. said Friday it holds a 9.1 percent stake in Consolidated Cigar Holdings Inc or 550,000 Class A common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it bought the stake between August 21 and August 29 at prices ranging from $28.31 and $31.61 per share.</p>
<p>The group said it bought the shares for investment purposes only.</p>
